linux-island (@VERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The popup no longer opens by itself when the pill grows under a resting
    pointer (a song starting, a volume or brightness pop-up); it opens once
    the pointer moves over the pill, or on a click.
  * Wayland sessions: the home card is left out, because native Wayland
    windows (recent Chrome, Brave, VS Code) can't be seen and the card would
    stay up; Settings says so.

 -- Linux Island maintainers <linux-island@localhost>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0530

linux-island (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Settings panel: monitors, colours, every feature on or off, screensaver
    and lock options, start on login; changes apply live.
  * Screensaver and lock: the pill swoops into a clock card and the screen
    fades to a black clock.
  * Event-driven window, volume and camera tracking (much lower CPU use).
  * Volume, brightness and battery icons follow their levels.

 -- Linux Island maintainers <linux-island@localhost>  Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0530
